{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1132"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c095): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c095.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1132"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-film-media__film.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",772],["+","Not every new name came from a studio office. Frederick Austerlitz, born in Omaha, Nebraska, in 1899, the son of an Austrian immigrant, was renamed by his own family when he and his sister Adele began dancing in vaudeville as children; the Austerlitz siblings became the Astaires. The pair were Broadway stars of the 1920s, and after Adele retired he went to Hollywood, where as Fred Astaire (1899-1987) he danced with Ginger Rogers in Top Hat and Swing Time and became the most admired dancer in film history.\n\n"],["=",95],["+","\n| Frederick Austerlitz | Fred Astaire |"],["=",74]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",732],["+","Nicht jeder neue Name kam aus einem Studiobüro. Frederick Austerlitz, 1899 in Omaha, Nebraska, als Sohn eines österreichischen Einwanderers geboren, wurde von seiner eigenen Familie umbenannt, als er und seine Schwester Adele schon als Kinder im Varieté zu tanzen begannen; aus den Geschwistern Austerlitz wurden die Astaires. Das Paar war in den 1920er-Jahren ein Broadway-Star, und nachdem Adele sich zurückgezogen hatte, ging er nach Hollywood, wo er als Fred Astaire (1899–1987) mit Ginger Rogers in „Ich tanz’ mich in dein Herz hinein“ und „Swing Time“ tanzte und zum meistbewunderten Tänzer der Filmgeschichte wurde.\n\n"],["=",91],["+","\n| Frederick Austerlitz | Fred Astaire |"],["=",70]]}]},
